I don't doubt in what you say about VE, I don't play that GUI/variant.

The point is that VE needs some meta-information about the weights.
Those could be obtained from the data in objects.c and stored in the
VE frontend to display the additional information once you've ID'ed
the item or resp. once you've picked it up so that you can tell apart
different items, e.g., of the same appearance. But if the interface
displays the weight even if those conditions are not met that means
that VE must itself have knowledge about the actual object which is
not possible to derive from the information provided by vanilla NH
on the user frontend. This weight is information meant to be hidden,
I presume, because it would otherwise make the loadstone concept
trivial to solve in the general case (including a stone in some
corner that you cannot kick). Showing that information beforehand
changes the game so that we would have to consider VE a variant.
I think it would be a good feature to display the weight, once the
object has been lifted, but the weight should not be displayed by
the variant/GUI without the player having obtained the necessary
information by in-game means.

